    "## 2. Operational definitions\n",
    "\n",
    "First pole = positive direction of the saved vector.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Vector | First pole | Second pole |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| factual/hallucinatory | supported by the reference, or abstains | adds unsupported claims |\n",
    "| serious/funny | sober, literal | humorous, playful |\n",
    "| casual/formal | conversational | polished, professional |\n",
    "| creative/empirical | speculative, imaginative | evidence-led, measured |\n",
    "| honest/sycophantic | keeps independent judgment | agrees to please |\n",
    "| confident/unsure | decisive | hedged, visibly uncertain |\n",
    "| empathetic/unempathetic | responds to emotion | emotionally detached |\n",
    "| calm/anxious | steady, reassuring | tense, worried |\n",
    "\n",
    "Caveats worth remembering when reading results:\n",
    "\n",
    "- creative ↔ empirical is a chosen stylistic axis, not a logical opposition\n",
    "- confident ↔ unsure measures *expressed* certainty, not warranted certainty\n",
    "- factual ↔ hallucinatory is closed-world — really grounded ↔ unsupported\n",
    "- honest ↔ sycophantic only covers resisting false user claims, not honesty generally"
   ]
  },
